'''Mythic Items''' are special one-piece [[ON:Sets|sets]] that can only be obtained through the [[ON:Antiquities|Antiquities]] system and if you have access to the related [[ON:DLC|DLC]]. Only '''one''' mythic item can be worn at a time, but they each grant powerful and unique bonuses. 

All mythic items are broken up into five fragments which each need to be found to create the final piece. All fragments require a legendary-quality [[ON:Antiquity Leads|Lead]] to [[ON:Scrying|scry]], and are classed as [[ON:Antiquity Leads#Master|Master difficulty]] to [[ON:Excavation|excavate]]. You are required to be at least level 7 in Scrying, and have the [[ON:Antiquarian Insight|Antiquarian Insight IV]] passive to scry Master difficulty leads.

Additional DLCs or [[ON:Chapters|Chapters]] may be required (including the DLC or Chapter the Mythic item was released alongside) to obtain each fragment. For example, the [[ON:Ring of the Pale Order|Ring of the Pale Order]] was released with the ''[[ON:Markarth|Markarth]]'' DLC, but it also requires access to the ''[[ON:Orsinium|Orsinium]]'' DLC to find all fragment Leads. In addition, the ''[[ON:Greymoor|Greymoor]]'' Chapter is ''also'' required to Scry these Leads via the [[ON:Scrying|Scrying]] skill line. The table below shows the DLCs required to complete a particular Mythic item. 

